  "raw": " Altoona on Oct. 8, 1952, the son of Donald and Rena (Perone) Gates Sr. Flip attended Devon High School and Muskingum Mills Mill township vocational school. He continued his education and received the GED certificate from Bridgeville Career Education Center. During the evacuations due to the hurricane, Flip served with the all volunteer Biloxi Marshalls for three years; he also formed a construction crew which helped broker new housing through the evacuees. In 1978, he met Patricia Birch who would eventually become his loving wife. On Dec. 1, 1984 he married Patricia Birch. They enjoyed spending time holidaying at their retirement home at Phoenix River Resort. Flip worked diligently alongside his sons, Bill Gates, Jr., and Aric Gates and proudly worked right along side them all over Fort Lauderdale Florida and the Carolinas until his health declined. He continued to serve by lending a hand and going \"all hands on deck\" on several occasions during hurricanes, flood rescues, sand",
  "serialized": "Altoona on Oct. 8, 1952, the son of Donald and Rena (Perone) Gates Sr. Flip attended Devon High School and Muskingum Mills Mill township vocational school. He continued his education and received the GED certificate from Bridgeville Career Education Center. During the evacuations due to the hurricane, Flip served with the all volunteer Biloxi Marshalls for three years; he also formed a construction crew which helped broker new housing through the evacuees. In 1978, he met Patricia Birch who would eventually become his loving wife. On Dec. 1, 1984 he married Patricia Birch. They enjoyed spending time holidaying at their retirement home at Phoenix River Resort. Flip worked diligently alongside his sons, Bill Gates, Jr., and Aric Gates and proudly worked right along side them all over Fort Lauderdale Florida and the Carolinas until his health declined. He continued to serve by lending a hand and going \"all hands on deck\" on several occasions during hurricanes, flood rescues, sand",
